From: Acer RGB Project <kbd-preset@localhost>
Date: Sat, 23 May 2026 19:28:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] DMI compatibility bypass for non-Clevo hardware

Bypass the DMI-based hardware compatibility check so that the
tuxedo-drivers keyboard backlight modules can load on laptops
that have a compatible ACPI WMI interface but are not in the
TUXEDO/Clevo vendor whitelist.

The tuxedo_keyboard module's init function calls this check and
refuses to load on hardware that isn't DMI-matched. However, the
WMI GUIDs used by clevo_wmi are standard Microsoft ACPI WMI GUIDs
present on all modern laptops, and the method-0x52 probe test
succeeds on any ACPI WMI implementation. The DMI check is the
sole gatekeeper preventing these modules from working on hardware
that has no actual incompatibility.

diff --git a/src/tuxedo_compatibility_check/tuxedo_compatibility_check.c b/src/tuxedo_compatibility_check/tuxedo_compatibility_check.c
index 7461c34..e7cd5e0 100644
--- a/src/tuxedo_compatibility_check/tuxedo_compatibility_check.c
+++ b/src/tuxedo_compatibility_check/tuxedo_compatibility_check.c
@@ -220,12 +220,7 @@ static const struct dmi_system_id tuxedo_dmi_string_match[] = {
 };
 
 bool tuxedo_is_compatible(void) {
-	if (dmi_check_system(tuxedo_dmi_string_match)
-	    || (x86_match_cpu(skip_tuxedo_dmi_string_check_match)
-	    && !x86_match_cpu(force_tuxedo_dmi_string_check_match))) {
-		return true;
-	}
-	return false;
+	return true;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(tuxedo_is_compatible);
 
